From: Havard Bjerke <haavabj@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] gallivm: use auto for the getHostCPUFeatures StringMap iterator

LLVM 22 reworked StringMap's iterators: the concrete class is now
StringMapIterBase<ValueTy, bool> and llvm::StringMapIterator no longer
exists, so the hardcoded llvm::StringMapIterator<bool> fails to compile:

  error: 'StringMapIterator' is not a member of 'llvm'; did you mean
  'StringMapKeyIterator'?

Only the DETECT_ARCH_ARM path uses this loop, so the breakage is limited
to 32-bit Arm targets. Use auto so the code builds against both the old
and the new StringMap API.

Upstream: not submitted
Signed-off-by: Havard Bjerke <haavabj@gmail.com>

--- a/src/gallium/auxiliary/gallivm/lp_bld_misc.cpp
+++ b/src/gallium/auxiliary/gallivm/lp_bld_misc.cpp
@@ -331,7 +331,7 @@
       llvm::sys::getHostCPUFeatures(features);
    #endif
 
-   for (llvm::StringMapIterator<bool> f = features.begin();
+   for (auto f = features.begin();
         f != features.end();
         ++f) {
       MAttrs.push_back(((*f).second ? "+" : "-") + (*f).first().str());
